  "notes": "Event dates in narrative span April 10-17, 2025; engineering evaluation (May 5, 2025) determined inoperability duration exceeded the 72-hour TS allowed outage time without RICT implementation, resulting in a condition prohibited by TS 3.7.3. Cause code A (Personnel Error) reflects the improperly installed gasket (legacy issue) and ineffective corrective actions following the 2008 bearing failure. Modeled the gasket-installation defect as the root FailureMode leading in parallel to both the observed oil leak and the partial line blockage, each of which independently contributed to the extended inoperability. Three previous similar LERs referenced only by date/description, not by LER number, so stub keys are synthesized placeholders pending resolver canonicalization; no explicit LER numbers were given in the narrative for these OE references."
